l by the lender;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- interest rate cost for USD drawn down is 9%;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- interest rate cost for UAH drawn down: 17.0% to 30 days, 17.50% 31 to 90 days, 20.00% 91 to 180 days, 21.00% 181 to 365 days;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- borrowing above UAH90m, equivalent to $3.3m at 30 June 2021 (2020: $3.2m) will require a corporate guarantee from \f28 \uc2 \f2 JKX Oil & Gas plc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The corporate guarantee provided by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 JKX Oil & Gas plc\f28 \uc2 \f2  in respect of the credit facility with Tascombank is considered to be an insurance contract under the provisions of IFRS 4;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JKX Oil & Gas PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  Half-year Report -11-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- assets with a market value of UAH460m, equivalent to $16.9m at 30 June 2021 (2020: UAH460m, equivalent to $16.3m) have been identified for use as a collateral, collateral is to be provided only on a drawdown; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- amount borrowed will be repaid during the last 4 months, by equal-sized monthly payments, to be effected on the last day of the month/the last day of the credit limit period. Last date of repayment for the last part of amount borrowed is 13 December 2021.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The credit facility of $10.3m (31 December 2020: $9.9m) includes two financial covenants. If the covenants are not met an additional interest of 2% applies to the facility but failure to meet covenants does not represent an event of default:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- to keep gross margin at no less than 50% during the period of the credit facility agreement, based on PPC's financial reporting results. This covenant was not met, however this did not result in additional interest of 2% being applied as the credit facility was not used during the period ended 30 June 2021.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- starting from the first quarter of 2019 and during the period of the credit facility agreement, PPC is to maintain the ratio between financial (interest) debt and EBITDA (adjusted to the annual value) at no more than 3.0. This covenant has been met as PPC had no debt during the period ended 30 June 2021.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In July 2020 PPC also signed a $5.0m loan facility agreement with Alfa-Bank valid for 3 years. The loan facility cannot exceed $5.0m, calculated at a fixed at the date of agreement exchange rate of $27.6647.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The main terms and conditions of the loan facility with Alfa-Bank are as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- drawdowns can be made either in USD, EUR or UAH and are individually subject to credit approval by the lender;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- interest rate cost for USD drawn down is 4.9%, based on 2 months repayment;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- interest rate cost for EUR drawn down 4.4%, based on 2 months repayment;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- interest rate cost for UAH drawn down 11.3%, based on 2 months repayment;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- full loan facility will require a corporate guarantee from JKX Oil & Gas plc. The corporate guarantee provided by the JKX Oil & Gas plc in respect of the credit facility with Alfa-Bank is considered to be an insurance contract under the provisions of IFRS 4;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- collateral shall be properly documented and provided in advance, the tranche cannot be granted otherwise; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 each amount borrowed shall be repaid within 2 months from the date when the tranche is agreed (agreed by signing of an additional agreement ). The last date of the agreed loan facility is 21 July 2023.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Significant financial penalties:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the non-payment penalty is 0.2% per day of the overdue amount but no more than National Bank of Ukraine (NBU) double discount rate;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- if the covenants are not met (for each case) an additional interest of 0.1% applies to the facility; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- if the amount of the loan facility is not used for the purpose indicated in the loan facility agreement PPC is liable to pay 25% of the amount used not for the purpose indicated in the loan facility agreement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Significant financial covenants:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All covenants listed below have been met during the period ended 30 June 2021.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- EBITDA - should not be less than Nil at the end of each quarter during the period of the loan facility agreement;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Debt to EBITDA ratio - should be no more than 3.0 at the end of each quarter during the period of the loan facility agreement; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EBITDA to Financial costs (Interest) ratio - should be not less than 2.0 at the end of each quarter during the period of the loan facility agreement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 8. Discontinued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and assets classified as held for sale\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In early February 2018 the Group announced its intention to exit its oil and gas \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Hungary and initiated an active programme to dispose of its Hungarian business.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On 9 March 2020 the company announced that it had agreed terms for the disposal of the entire share capital of Hungarian business. Following pandemic related delays the Group received notification that the relevant Hungarian authorities had refused the necessary consent to the transaction pursuant to legislation introduced as a result of the current COVID-19 pandemic. Consequently, the transaction did not proceed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hungarian business unit has been classified as held for sale for the period of more than 12 months.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An extension of the period required to complete the sale does not preclude the asset from being classified as held for sale as the delay is caused by events and circumstances beyond the Group's control. Managemen