ere identified in relation to the Group's assets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 6. Other receivable\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The non-current receivable consists of VAT recoverable as a result of expenditures incurred in Russia. The receivable is expected to be recovered between two and five years (2016: two and five years).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7. Cash \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                             1 January         Net  30 June \par                                  2017    movement     2017 \par                                  $000        $000     $000 \par Cash                          8,874     (5,296)     3,578 \par Short term deposits           5,193     (4,760)      433 \par --------------------------  ---------  ----------  ------- \par Cash and cash equivalents    14,067     (10,056)    4,011 \par Restricted cash                201         17        218 \par --------------------------  ---------  ----------  ------- \par Total                        14,268     (10,039)    4,229 \par --------------------------  ---------  ----------  ------- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Short term deposits comprise amounts which are held on deposit, but are readily convertible to cash.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Restricted cash\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 30 June 2017 $0.2m (31 December 2016: $0.2m) of the cash held in Hungary at K & H Bank Zrt was restricted as under the Hungarian Mining Act the Group is required to deposit cash to cover compensation for any land damage and the costs of recultivation, including environmental damage of the waste management facilities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 8. Borrowings \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                     30 June  30 June \par                                                       31 December \par                                        2017     2016         2016 \par                                        $000     $000         $000 \par Current \par Convertible bonds due 2020 (2016: \par  2018) (1)     