rrent provisions                                                                     $000 \par -------------------------------  --------------------------  ----------  ----------  ------ \par At 1 January 2017                                         -     589        33,921    34,510 \par Foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  translation                 -                   28        1,453     1,481 \par Amount provided / (utilised)in \par  the period/year                           1,440               (184)       1,824     3,080 \par -------------------------------  --------------------------  ----------  ----------  ------ \par At 30 June 2017                            1,440                433        37,198    39,071 \par -------------------------------  --------------------------  ----------  ----------  ------ \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1. The provision for production based taxes, which had been recognised as a charge in the 2016 and 2015 Consolidated income statements, is in respect of a claim against PPC for additional Rental Fees for the period January to December 2015 and August to December 2010 respectively. Both claims are being contested in the Ukrainian courts (see Note 14). The amount is denominated in Ukrainian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hryvnia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ('UAH') and is stated above at its US$-equivalent amount using exchange rate at 30 June 2017 of UAH26.10/$ (31 December 2016: UAH 27.19/$). The provision is based on the total value of the claims plus interest and penalties. The Board believes that the claims are without merit under Ukrainian law and the Company will continue to contest it vigorously. No contingent liabilities exist in respect of Ukrainian production taxes (31 December 2016: nil).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2. The onerous lease provision covers the Group's liability for onerous lease contracts relating to London office. Following reduction in London office staff, two out of the four