t exceeds by $2.0m and therefore HMP's assets were impaired due to the reduction in the estimated recoverable oil and gas volumes from this field.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par JKX Oil & Gas PLC Final Results to 31 December -16-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Any impairment is dependent on judgement used in determining the most appropriate basis for the assumptions and estimates made by management, particularly in relation to the key assumptions described above. Sensitivity analysis to likely and potential changes in key assumptions has therefore been reviewed below.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The impact on the impairment calculation of applying different assumptions to production, oil and gas prices and future capital and operating costs, all other inputs remaining equal, would be as follows: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                                                HMP \par                                                (Increase)/decrease \par                                                      in impairment \par                                                           of $2.0m \par                                                        for HMP CGU \par                                                                 $m \par -------------------------  -----------------  -------------------- \par Impact if oil and \par  gas prices:               increased by 10%           0.5 \par  decreased by 10%                                    (0.5) \par  -------------------------------------------  -------------------- \par Impact if oil and \par  gas production volumes:   increased by 10%           0.5 \par  decreased by 10%                                    (0.5) \par  -------------------------------------------  -------------------- \par Impact if future \par  capital and operating \par  costs:                    increased by 10%          (0.4) \par  decreased by 10%                                     0.4 \par  -------------------------------------------  ---