\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  to switch to closed-circle  \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 2016\par 17:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Oct 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will in future sell dollars directly to a limited circle of banks rather than at open auctions, an official said on Monday, in a bid to combat speculative trades against the under-pressure \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  more effectively.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has traditionally defended the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  by offering foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at auctions that are announced in advance and open to all lenders.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has slipped to 25 against the dollar from 8 since 2014, battered by two years of economic crisis and conflict with Russian-backed separatists in the country's east, and inflation jumped to 20-year high in 2015.\par \par \uc2 "We plan to launch a faster and more secret tool to respond problems, speculative attacks on the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", Serhii Ponomarenko, director of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  department, told journalists.\par \par \uc2 He said it took hours to announce and conduct an auction while direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be done in minutes.\par \par \uc2 "There will not be any announcement in advance. We will simply submit our request directly to 15-20 banks (the biggest market players) asking them about their quotes ... and then - we will get a deal at the best price," he said.\par \par \uc2 He said such hidden \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would help make better use of \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to abandon its fixed exchange rate policy at the start of 2015 when its international reserves fell to $5.6 billion, barely covering one month of imports.\par \par \uc2 Reserves had increased to $15.6 billion as of Oct. 1 mainly due to \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  loans. Kiev has received $7.7 billion of $17.5 billion that the Fund has promised to disburse in support of economic reforms.\par \par \uc2 Corruption remains the main obstacle to the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflow Ukraine needs to cover its current account deficit, pay debts and boost international reserves.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Natalia Zinets; editing by John Stonestreet) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-10-17T16:15:59.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020161017ecah00o8a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
