\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine central bank intervention \highlight\uc2  appears to stabilise  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2015\par 18:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Updates after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sale details announced)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Feb 26 (Reuters) - \uc2 Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars on Thursday for the same price it had paid for them the previous day, action that appeared to help stabilise its \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  somewhat after dramatic falls earlier in the week.\par \par \uc2 The dollar sales came after the bank abruptly lifted a one-day ban on nearly all commercial \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, which it had imposed just as suddenly on Wednesday morning.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it sold $81.89 million at a rate of 28.046 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar on Thursday. It had bought $80 million at the same rate during Wednesday's ban, which prohibited trading by banks for their clients and which it subsequently lifted after having said it would be in place for the rest of the week.\par \par \uc2 The repeated unexpected moves by the bank have sown confusion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Wednesday's ban on trading had drawn a rebuke from Prime Minister Arseny Yatseniuk.\par \par \uc2 The scarcity of commercial trading on Wednesday made it difficult to speak of a day-to-day rise or fall. But trades registered on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's website took place on Thursday at an average rate of 30.173, making the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  4.8 percent stronger than on Tuesday, the last day of unrestricted trade.\par \par \uc2 Several bank traders, speaking on condition of anonymity required by their employers, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been trading at a rate between 32 and 34 before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped in with its offer to sell dollars, boosting the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one of the worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world, has shed half its value over the course of this year after halving during the whole of 2014. (Reporting by Natalia Zinets; Writing by Peter Graff; Editing by Toby Chopra and Robin Pomeroy) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-2-26T18:19:01.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150226eb2q00b9f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
