\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine central bank \highlight\uc2 : decision on  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  doesn't mean  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  free float\b0\par\par\uc2 122 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2015\par 10:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Feb 5 (Reuters) - The head of \uc2 Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday the bank's decision not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market does not mean a free float of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Valeriia Gontareva, the bank's governor, told a news conference bank would simply allow for a greater fluctuation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and added: "Get used to market volatility."\par \par \uc2 She added that she hopes that the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  will finalise a decision on boosting financial aid to Kiev on Feb. 6-7. (Reporting by Natalia Zinets and Katya Golubkova, Writing in Moscow by Lidia Kelly, Editing by Timothy Heritage) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-2-5T10:20:18.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150205eb2500al3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
