\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-"Panic" pushing Ukraine's  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  to near record lows - Cbank chief\b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2014\par 17:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quote on reasonable \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, background)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Aug 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to offset a "mood of panic" over the separatist conflict pressuring the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which fell close to an all-time low against the dollar on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  slumped to 13.40 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar from 12.95 - its biggest daily move since April when pro-Russian separatists first seized control in Ukraine's eastern regions, sparking a conflict with government forces.\par \par \uc2 "Everyone understands that there are no economic factors ..., this is a mood of panic," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head Valeria Hontareva told parliament, promising the bank would continue market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The rate has moved really far from a reasonable level, even taking into account the military conflict a reasonable level today should be 11.50-11.90 to the dollar," she said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which started 2014 at close to 8.20 against the dollar, weakened to 13.70 in mid-April when rebels in the Russian-speaking east seized buildings and strategic points, declaring "people's republics" and saying they wanted union with Russia.\par \par \uc2 Financial aid from international lenders helped the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around 11-12 in May, but fears over the mounting economic and human costs of the conflict have hit the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks. (Reporting by Natalia Zinets; Writing by Alessandra Prentice; Editing by Richard Balmforth)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-8-15T15:00:50.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140812ea8c008vh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
