\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Russian stocks track emerging equities higher, rouble back in red\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sujata Rao   \par \uc2 568 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 11:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 18 (Reuters) - Russia's rouble fell on Tuesday from the previous session's two-week highs on fears of fresh economic sanctions and a further military standoff, though Moscow equities firmed in line with other emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 Equities were generally stronger across emerging markets, lifted by big gains in Indian and Korea, while Russian shares extended the 3.6 percent rise posted on Monday after Western sanctions were seen as milder than expected.\par \par \uc2 But Moscow's defiant move towards formally annexing the Crimea region is keeping alive tensions with the West. President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  is expected to back absorbing the territory into Russia when he addresses parliament later in the day.\par \par \uc2 HSBC\uc2  strategist Murat Toprak said investors would scan Putin's speech for clues as to whether military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely for the rest of \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The rouble weakened 0.6 percent against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The Crimea election is a done deal, the market wants to know if there is any intention to go beyond Crimea. This is one of the concerns of the market," Toprak said.\par \par \uc2 Fears the West will respond with fresh, more stringent sanctions are reflected in the offshore rouble forwards, which continue to trade at a rare premium to onshore contracts on fears that future local settlements could prove difficult.\par \par \uc2 In neighbouring Ukraine, the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell more than 4 percent to the dollar. Investors are waiting to see the result of an IMF mission to Kiev which concludes on Friday. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility is one of the IMF's demands.\par \par \uc2 "What happens to \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  depends on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and given the level of their \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves I'd expect that authorities would not stand in the way of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said RBS analyst Tatiana Orlova.\par \par \uc2 "On the basis of fundamentals, \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  should move to 11 or 12 per dollar."\par \par \uc2 While broader emerging markets have been boosted by better economic data from many countries, including the so-called Fragile Five, gains were seen capped by Chinese developments.\par \par \uc2 The yuan traded almost at one-year lows to the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weekend move to widen its trading band, indicating it was willing to tolerate more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility. Traders expect more weakness as the economy loses steam.\par \par \uc2 "The China backdrop is not very supportive - all these uncertainties about potential bankruptcies - this is a market concern, it's not very positive for emerging markets," Toprak said, referring to recent corporate difficulties.\par \par \uc2 Chinese stocks ended flat but MSCI's emerging markets index rose 0.2 percent, buoyed by gains in Seoul which posted the biggest one-day rise in two weeks and in Mumbai where foreign buyers pushed shares to record highs before elections.\par \par \uc2 Overseas funds have bought a net $1.6 billion worth of Indian shares in the past 20 sessions, while \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  upped its recommendation on Indian shares to overweight.\par \par \uc2 Turkish equities were a quarter point higher but the lira fell 0.4 percent ahead of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting that is expected to leave interest rates unchanged. The bank jacked up all its interest rates by 250-500 basis points at the end of January to protect the lira.\par \par \uc2 \f2               \par               \par               \par               \par               \par For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par               \par For TURKISH market report, see\par \par               \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For RUSSIAN market report, see )\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-3-21T10:51:45.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140318ea3i00bym\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 Dukascopy Bank SA Research Division: Yen drops most in two weeks since Ukraine risks ease\b0\par\par\uc2 527 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par \uc2 News Bites - Private Companies\par \uc2 NBPRCO\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014. News Bites Pty Ltd.   \par \par \uc2 NEWS BITES - PRIVATE COMPANIES\par \par \uc2 [Company Release]\par \par \uc2 The Japanese Yen fell to the lowest point in two weeks against the Dollar since president of Russia, Vladimir Putin, stated that no direct necessity is needed to send forces to Ukraine, thus curbing safe asset demand. The Yen declined against all of the 16 major peers, while the Ruble gained. Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciated 0.4% to 101.85 against the Dollar at 6:51 a.m. in NY, sliding to the lowest decline since February 18 and dropped 0.6% to 140.19 versus the Euro, which allowed the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen 0.2% to $1.3764.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/marketwatch/market_news/Market-News-and-Research/41182/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 BUSINESS NEWS ROUND UP\par \par \uc2 04 March 2014: Dukascopy Bank SA Research Division: Brent falls after rising yesterday on Ukraine's easing tension\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] The European benchmark Brent crude slipped on Tuesday session after rising notable yesterday as the Russian Federation entered Ukraine's Crimea peninsula, however war conflict is unlikely to happen according to experts. Brent for delivery in April fell 1.9%, or $2.09, to $109.11 per barrel on the London's ICE Futures Europe exchange. Source: Company Website\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/marketwatch/market_news/Market-News-and-Research/41192/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 04 March 2014: Dukascopy Bank SA Research Division: WTI slips as Russia-Ukraine tension eases\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] West Texas Intermediate oil declined on Tuesday trading session falling from the strongest level since September on speculation that the escalating geopolitical tension between the Russian Federation and Ukraine is unlikely to end up in a war conflict. WTI for settlement in April slipped $1.62 to $103.30 per barrel on the NYMEX and was last seen at $103.69 by 1:29 p.m.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/marketwatch/market_news/Market-News-and-Research/41191/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 03 March 2014: Dukascopy Bank SA Research Division: \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls to record low as Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine currency Hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined on Monday trading session falling towards the lowest level all-time after the Russian Federation \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  into \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Crimea peninsula raising concerns over possible war conflict as the Russian President Putin declares his troops had right to enter the country.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/marketwatch/market_news/Market-News-and-Research/41103/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 03 March 2014: Dukascopy Bank SA Research Division: U.S. shares fall on Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] Wall Street edged lower on Monday trading session together with most risk assets world-wide after Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  raising concerns over possible war conflict as the President of Russian Federation Vladimir Putin claimed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was correct.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/marketwatch/market_news/Market-News-and-Research/41100/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 03 March 2014: Dukascopy Bank SA Research Division: Bank of Russia raises rates by 150 basis points\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Russian increased its benchmark interest rates unexpectedly on Monday amid raising concerns over possible war conflict in neighboring Ukraine pushing the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Ruble towards the historical low versus the U.S. Dollar. The Bank of Russia raised the rate by 150 basis points from 5.50% to 7.00%. Source: Company Website\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/marketwatch/market_news/Market-News-and-Research/41104/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 Dokument NBPRCO0020140305ea35001a2\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 Dukascopy Bank SA Research Division: Dollar rises as investors seek for safe-haven\b0\par\par\uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par \uc2 News Bites - Private Companies\par \uc2 NBPRCO\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014. News Bites Pty Ltd.   \par \par \uc2 NEWS BITES - PRIVATE COMPANIES\par \par \uc2 [Company Release]\par \par \uc2 U.S. Dollar advanced on Monday trading session together with the Japanese Yen as investors seek for safe-haven assets after the Russian Federation entered Ukraine's Crimea peninsula raising political tension in the country. The so-called Greenback increased pushing the Dollar index 0.3% higher to 79.885, while the Yen added as much as 0.6% against the Euro to 139.67.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/marketwatch/market_news/Market-News-and-Research/41101/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 BUSINESS NEWS ROUND UP\par \par \uc2 03 March 2014: Dukascopy Bank SA Research Division: \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls to record low as Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine currency Hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined on Monday trading session falling towards the lowest level all-time after the Russian Federation \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  into \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Crimea peninsula raising concerns over possible war conflict as the Russian President Putin declares his troops had right to enter the country.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/marketwatch/market_news/Market-News-and-Research/41103/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 03 March 2014: Dukascopy Bank SA Research Division: U.S. personal spending and income both advance in January\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] Personal spending and income in the U.S. increased in January at a notable faster pace than experts originally estimated, a report published by the Commerce Department showed on Monday. According to the report, the U.S. personal income gained 0.3% in January compared to a 0.2% jump estimated earlier, while personal spending climbed 0.4% in the same month. Source: Company Website\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/marketwatch/market_news/Market-News-and-Research/41108/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 03 March 2014: Dukascopy Bank SA Research Division: Bank of Russia raises rates by 150 basis points\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Russian increased its benchmark interest rates unexpectedly on Monday amid raising concerns over possible war conflict in neighboring Ukraine pushing the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Ruble towards the historical low versus the U.S. Dollar. The Bank of Russia raised the rate by 150 basis points from 5.50% to 7.00%. Source: Company Website\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/marketwatch/market_news/Market-News-and-Research/41104/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 03 March 2014: Dukascopy Bank SA Research Division: U.S. construction spending rises slower in January\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] Construction spending in the world's largest economy surprisingly eased at the beginning of 2014, however it stayed in positive territory suggesting that the sector is growing, a report released by the Commerce Department showed on Monday. The U.S. construction spending advanced 0.1% rising from December's level of $941.9 billion to a level of $943.1 billion recorded in January. Source: Company Website\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/marketwatch/market_news/Market-News-and-Research/41107/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 03 March 2014: Dukascopy Bank SA Research Division: Portugal industrial output rises slower in January\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] Industrial production in Portugal advanced at the beginning of 2014, however the pace of growth was lower than economists preliminary estimated, a data published by the statistical office unveiled on Monday. The country's industrial output gained 3.9% on an annual basis in January after rising by 5.7% in the last month of 2013. Source: Company Website\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/marketwatch/market_news/Market-News-and-Research/41106/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 Dokument NBPRCO0020140304ea34001xq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
