\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Ukraine debt insurance costs soar, Latam assets sink\b0\par\par\uc2 By Asher Levine and Natsuko Waki   \par \uc2 570 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2014\par 16:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO/LONDON, Feb 13 (Reuters) - Growing fears of a default pushed Ukraine's debt-insurance costs to four-year highs on Thursday, while concern over economic growth and inflation drove Latin American assets lower.\par \par \uc2 Higher \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields also weighed on emerging markets, bringing losses in South Africa's rand, the Turkish lira, Russian rouble and Hungarian forint , some of the worst-hit \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the sell-off that began last month. Nigeria's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounded, however, following a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Concern has been growing over how \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  can prop up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pay off its debt. Russia suspended a $15 billion bailout after Ukrainian President Viktor Yanukovich sacked his prime minister late last month.\par \par \uc2 "Ukraine is on the knife-edge of solvency risk," said Gabriel Sterne, an economist at broker Exotix.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  brought in temporary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls last week after the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell below 9 per dollar for the first time in five years. The bank said on Thursday controls may last longer than two weeks, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to fall.\par \par \uc2 Investors were not convinced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could continue to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened further on Thursday, losing 1.5 percent against the dollar, and Ukraine's 5-year credit default swaps rose further, gaining 116 basis points from Wednesday's close to 1,241 bps, according to Markit.\par \par \uc2 Hungary's forint fell 0.8 percent to 311.75. Investors are watching inflation data due Friday for clues on whether rates will be cut again next week. Hungary's benchmark rate is already at a record-low 2.85 percent.\par \par \uc2 Higher \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields weighed on sentiment as investors moved money from emerging-market assets into the recovering U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark emerging equity index fell 1 percent, with Chinese, Indian and Russian shares all weaker.\par \par \uc2 In Latin America, both Brazil's real and Mexico's peso weakened slightly. MSCI's Latin American stock index fell the most in more than a week.\par \par \uc2 A proposed increase in consumer electricity rates has heightened inflation expectations in Brazil, where yields on interest rate futures ticked higher Thursday. Weaker-than- expected retail sales also sapped risk appetite.\par \par \uc2 "Some calculations now suggest gross domestic product could fall into negative territory in the fourth quarter, something that was (previously) out of the question," said Gustavo Mendonca, an economist with Saga Capital in Rio de Janeiro.\par \par \uc2 A plunge in \uc2 Banco do Brasil SA\uc2  shares helped drag Brazilian stocks down. The state-run lender posted worse-than-expected quarterly earnings and signalled a possible slowdown in lending this year.\par \par \uc2 Mexican shares also dropped, following weak earnings from conglomerate Alfa.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the Nigerian naira rebounded from a two-year low against the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold an undisclosed amount of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lenders to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Nigerian stocks and bonds got hammered earlier in the session as investors sold off frontier-market assets.\par \par \uc2 Africa's second-largest economy and biggest oil producer has been a top frontier-market investment in recent years. But political instability is a concern before upcoming elections, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tightened reserve requirements.\par \par \uc2 \f2               \par               \par               \par               \par               \par               \par For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par               \par For TURKISH market report, see\par \par               \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For RUSSIAN market report, see\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-2-16T15:44:46.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140213ea2d00ogl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
