\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Stocks rise nearly 1 pct on China data, Ukraine rates jump\b0\par\par\uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2013\par 12:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 9 (Reuters) - Emerging stocks rose nearly 1 percent on Monday on strong Chinese data, while Ukraine's short-term interest rates jumped as political unrest put pressure on the country's assets.\par \par \uc2 Asian shares rallied after data showed Chinese exports rose an above-forecast 12.7 percent from a year earlier, according to figures on the world's second biggest economy released on Sunday, and the trade surplus widened.\par \par \uc2 "The resilience of the Chinese economy...is likely to boost emerging market exports, especially considering...\b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have largely depreciated this year, which effectively restored a good part of EM economies' competitiveness," said analysts at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  in a client note.\par \par \uc2 The MSCI emerging equities index rose 0.8 percent to six-day highs, though Chinese shares were steady.\par \par \uc2 Indian stocks rose 1.5 percent to a record high after the main opposition party BJP, widely seen as being more business friendly, scored big wins on Sunday in three out of four key state elections held since last month.\par \par \uc2 China's yuan hit a record high after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  relaxed its grip on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the data.\par \par \uc2 The yuan has appreciated 2.6 percent so far this year, compared with a 1 percent rise in 2012.\par \par \uc2 Emerging market assets remained generally buoyant despite strong U.S. employment data on Friday, which brought forward some expectations of a withdrawal of the U.S. monetary stimulus that has helped risky assets.\par \par \uc2 In Ukraine, short-term interest rates soared to their highest for a year on intensifying political pressure.\par \par \uc2 One-week rates rose as high as 18 percent, according to Reuters data, up from 7 percent on Friday, and 3.5 percent a week ago.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell sharply in November, data showed on Friday, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit six-week highs in the spot market on Monday, however, with one local dealer saying there was a shortage in the market.\par \par \uc2 Ishitaa Sharma, emerging markets strategist at Citi, said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had also helped support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days, "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  but it is becoming more aggressive now."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forward rates were under pressure, but remained below recent elevated levels. Debt insurance costs also remained at distressed levels near 1,100 basis points (bps) for five-year credit default swaps, according to Markit.\par \par \uc2 Emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were flat to slightly weaker, with the rand edging away from 4-1/2 year lows set last week. Emerging sovereign debt spreads edged out 2 bps to 353 bps over U.S. Treasuries.\par \par \uc2 (For GRAPHIC on MSCI emerging index performance 2013, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/weh36s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/weh36s}}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on MSCI emerging Europe performance 2013, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jun28s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jun28s}}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on MSCI frontier index performance 2013, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/zyh97s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/zyh97s}}}\par \par \uc2 For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par \uc2 For TURKISH market report, see\par \par \uc2 For RUSSIAN market report, see ) (Reporting by Carolyn Cohn and Sujata Rao in London and Natalia Zinets in Kiev; Editing by Louise Ireland)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING | AFN | GFN | GBN | ABN | M | D | C | GRO | MTL | SOF | O | OIL | SNI | SNS | SI | IF | RBN | E | Z | RNP | DNP | PTD | PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131212e9c9000k6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
