\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Russia urges order in Ukraine as gas talks begin\b0\par\par\uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2013\par 11:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW/KIEV, Dec 4 (Reuters) - Russia called on Wednesday for "stability and order" in neighbouring Ukraine as the two countries held their first high-level talks since Kiev pulled out of a trade alliance with the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister \uc2 Dmitry Medvedev\uc2  hosted a Ukrainian delegation led by a deputy prime minister, Yuri Boiko, that is seeking cheaper gas and financial aid to close gaping external deficits that could set off a balance of payments crisis.\par \par \uc2 Risks of a financial meltdown in Ukraine, a former Soviet state of 46 million, became acute after mass demonstrations in Kiev last weekend against President Viktor Yanukovich and his government over a decision to seek closer alliance with Moscow.\par \par \uc2 "You are having quite an active political season," Medvedev told Boiko in a meeting at his residence outside Moscow, according to the \uc2 Interfax\uc2  news agency.\par \par \uc2 "Of course this is an internal matter, but it is very important that there be stability and order in the country."\par \par \uc2 Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  had threatened financial sanctions against Kiev if it signed a trade agreement with the EU last week. Yanukovich abandoned the deal at the last moment, surprising European leaders and angering domestic critics.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian Prime Minister \uc2 Mykola Azarov\uc2  told his cabinet that the Boiko visit would continue a dialogue with Russia on trade and economic relations that are "very critical for maintaining and developing Ukrainian industry and economy."\par \par \uc2 The Boiko visit was clearly part of the government's plans to sketch out what the Ukrainians hope will be a 'roadmap' for future economic ties with their old Soviet master.\par \par \uc2 No immediate breakthroughs were announced but Yanukovich, who was visiting China, was expected to meet Putin soon.\par \par \uc2 Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov said Putin would not meet Boiko. No date had yet been set for an encounter between the two presidents.\par \par \uc2 GAS PAYMENTS\par \par \uc2 Adding to the pressure on Ukraine, the CEO of Russian gas export monopoly \uc2 Gazprom\uc2 , \uc2 Alexei Miller\uc2 , said no deal had been reached to put off payment of any portion of Kiev's debt for gas deliveries this year.\par \par \uc2 "We are seeking options to resolve this issue, we are holding talks, but no agreements have been reached at this point," Miller said in a statement. He said Ukraine owes just over $2 billion for August, October and November.\par \par \uc2 The head of Ukraine's state-run energy firm Naftogaz, \uc2 Yevhen Bakulin\uc2 , had been quoted as saying on Tuesday that it had agreed with \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  to defer payments for the final three months of 2013 until spring.\par \par \uc2 Bakulin also said Naftogaz would pay $765 million due to \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  for deliveries in August.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine faces huge problems to finance a current account deficit of 7 percent of gross domestic product. Cheaper Russian gas would buy time for Kiev to find ways to meet outside funding needs estimated at $17 billion next year.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the value of the national \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , amid concerns that its stock of foreign reserves of $20 billion will be sufficient to hold the line.\par \par \uc2 The cost of insuring Ukrainian government debt for five years rose to 1,097 basis points, near-four-year highs. Levels over 1,000 basis points are indicative of financial distress.\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE/RUSSIA-GAS (UPDATE 3, PICTURE) | G | RBN | RNA | AFA | CSA | LBY | RWSA | RWS | REULB | GNS | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | ABX | BNX | FUN | RNP | PGE | SXNA   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131204e9c4000f2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
