\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Ukraine  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  Sept  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2  sales highest this year\b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Oktober 2011\par 11:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Maintaining the dollar peg is becoming costly\par \par \uc2 * Forwards point to devaluation in the coming months\par \par \uc2 * IMF programme key for supporting 2012 BoP - analyst\par \par \uc2 (Updates cbank \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales figure, adds retail purchase figure in paragraph 9)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Oct 10 (Reuters) - Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday its net foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales jumped to $2.0 billion in September, the highest monthly figure this year, as pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased.\par \par \uc2 The bank's reserves dropped by $3.3 billion last month to $35 billion as it stepped up \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank market.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is using up \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves pretty fast," Citi emerging markets strategist Luis Costa said.\par \par \uc2 "The market is already expecting a much higher dollar-\b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate in the next three to six months."\par \par \uc2 Non-deliverable forward contracts put the rate at 9.0/9.4 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  per dollar in three months and 9.8/10.4 in six months, down from the current level of 8.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement it had also supported payments made by state energy firm Naftogaz, which imports gas from Russia to distribute domestically.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official rate against the dollar weakened by 0.03 percent in September, the bank said. At the same time, the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened by 9.45 percent against the Russian rouble and by 5.44 percent against the euro.\par \par \uc2 Russia and the EU are Ukraine's main trade partners and analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have to allow some \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation soon.\par \par \uc2 However, the bank has said it wanted to maintain exchange rate stability to avoid panic on the retail market. In September, retail customers bought $2.1 billion net.\par \par \uc2 Citi's Costa said that Ukraine's balance of payments appeared stable in the short term, but renewing co-\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the International Monetary Fund was key for 2012.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine was due to receive about $6 billion from the IMF this year to boost \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves but the Fund halted disbursements after the government delayed unpopular reforms such as raising household gas prices.\par \par \uc2 An IMF mission is due to visit Kiev later this month.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Olzhas Auyezov; Editing by Anna Willard)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2   (UPDATE 3)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111010e7aa000k8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
