\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Ukraine c.bank sells dollars, buys euros\b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2010\par 13:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * First time this year c. bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in euros\par \par \uc2 * C. bank move supports \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Releads with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  adviser's comments)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Oct 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, selling dollars and buying euros, a senior adviser at the bank said.\par \par \uc2 "We fulfilled our intentions: we sold dollars in order to prevent volatility (in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) and bought euros in order to strengthen our reserve position," the adviser, Valeriy Lytvytsky, told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 He declined to give the volumes involved.\par \par \uc2 "We strengthened our foreign reserves because we bought \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more strongly than we sold," he said.\par \par \uc2 The bank at the start of trading offered to sell dollars at 7.9420 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> per dollar, compared with 7.9425 last Tuesday, and to buy the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 7.9099 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  per dollar <NBU01>, compared with 7.9100 on Oct 5.\par \par \uc2 It offered to sell euros at 11.0679 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> per euro in its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the Interbank market this year, with a buy rate of 11.0233 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  per euro.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said interbank quotes for the hyrvnia to the dollar remained unchanged.\par \par \uc2 "Despite the fact that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was selling at 7.9420/$ the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained at the level of 7.95/$. This means that there was some unsatisfied demand for dollars," one dealer said. (Reporting by Natalya Zinets; Writing by Richard Balmforth; Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-CBANK/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101012e6ac000qx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
