\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  c.bank sees  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  roughly stable\b0\par\par\uc2 539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 2010\par 11:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * C.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has halted \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall\par \par \uc2 * Adjusts \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate\par \par \uc2 * But sees little appreciation potential in the long run (Adds c.bank comment)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Sept 9 (Reuters) - Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , seeking to clarify its policy towards the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> exchange rate following a slew of mixed signals, said on Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would remain broadly stable against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The bank, which has stepped in this week to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said its chairman Volodymyr Stelmakh's earlier comments suggesting future depreciation had been misunderstood.\par \par \uc2 Stelmakh said on Wednesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which now trades at about 7.92 per dollar, would probably slip to 7.98-8.0 to the dollar by the end of 2010. [ID:nLDE6871AF]\par \par \uc2 But his senior advisor Valery Lytvytsky told Reuters on Thursday the figure was a floor for possible devaluation rather than a forecast of the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 "Volodymyr Stelmakh has said (the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) would not go lower than that but that does not mean it cannot perform better and it can perform better," Lytvytsky said.\par \par \uc2 Separately, the Ukrainsky Novyny news agency quoted Stelmakh as telling a meeting of government officials and regional governors on Thursday: "The (exchange) rate ... will be stable. (...) Of course, we do not foresee a large appreciation."\par \par \uc2 Stelmakh did not say what time frame he was referring to but made his comments in a speech covering the bank's outlook for the next year.\par \par \uc2 "I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to send the right signal to the market," said Renaissance Capital analyst Anastasia Golovach. "They are saying they will allow more \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility and I think this is good for the economy."\par \par \uc2 Allowing greater exchange rate flexibility is one of the terms of Ukraine's $15 billion deal with the International Monetary Fund agreed in July.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered to sell dollars at 7.9200 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  per dollar <NBU01>, down from 7.9269, the rate it had used on Tuesday and Wednesday to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> which has been volatile since Sept. 1.\par \par \uc2 The bank has sold $133 million on the interbank market so far this week.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar is weakening (against the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), the quotes are still close to where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is selling but we may go even lower," said a dealer at a large Ukrainian bank.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to 7.9150 per dollar on Thursday from 7.9265 at the end of the previous session, according to Reuters data, recovering further from a five-month low of 7.94 hit earlier in the week.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's steady appreciation during the summer came to a halt after a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reshuffle on Sept. 1 when Stelmakh's first deputy Anatoly Shapovalov replaced by younger banker Serhiy Arbuzov and prompted speculation of a change in the bank's stance towards the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The devaluation, although very small compared to overall gains since February, has drawn analysts' attention as a potential signal of a longer-term shift. [ID:nLDE68519F] (Reporting by Natalya Zinets, writing by Olzhas Auyezov; Editing by Susan Fenton)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100909e699000li\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
