\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  as  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  hits 2-mth low\b0\par\par\uc2 769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 2010\par 12:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits 2-month low vs dollar at 7.914\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offers to sell dollars at 7.9082\par \par \uc2 * Investors worried c.bank may be less keen on appreciation\par \par \uc2 * Monthly Naftogaz dollar purchases add pressure\par \par \uc2 (Recasts with c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 By Natalia Zinets and Olzhas Auyezov\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Sept 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> on Friday, two days after the replacement of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official prompted selling pressure that was spurred by state firm Naftogaz buying dollars.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped steady the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 7.914 per dollar according to Reuters data, its weakest since early July. That puts the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  on track for its biggest weekly slump since April with losses of 0.4 percent.\par \par \uc2 The sharp move prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to update its dedicated Reuters page for the first time since Tuesday <NBU01>, indicating it was ready to sell dollars at 7.9082 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A trader at a Western bank in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  had taken place.\par \par \uc2 The sell off began after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's First Deputy Chairman Anatoly Shapovalov, who was closely involved with exchange rate decision-making, resigned on Wednesday to be replaced by Serhiy Arbuzov, a banker with no prior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  experience.\par \par \uc2 Arbuzov is seen as an ally of President Valdimir Yanukovich and investors are concerned that he may be less keen on a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which hurts powerful exporters such as steelmaker Metinvest.\par \par \uc2 "It is highly likely the NBU will put more effort in preventing the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening excessively as the business entities that support the current president mostly represent large exporters and are not interested in \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthening," Alexander Pecherytsyn, analyst at ING, said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Investors who had previously bet on a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  "were probably frightened that the change of deputy governor at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be followed by a shift in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," said a dealer at a major bank.\par \par \uc2 "They started to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which added to demand from Naftogaz."\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian gas giant needs the dollars to pay for gas purchases from Russia's \uc2 Gazprom\uc2  . For July's imports, it owes around $780 million, although Prime Minister Mykola Azarov said on Friday the country would like to renegotiate its contracts to pay less in the future. [ID:nLDE6820TB]\par \par \uc2 "I think the growing demand (for dollars) is the work of Naftogaz, which traditionally needs to pay for imported gas by the seventh of the month," said one market participant.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's current account, which moved into deficit in July, may also keep downward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Irina Piantkovskaya, economist at Troika Dialog in Kiev.\par \par \uc2 STABILITY TO COME?\par \par \uc2 Credit derivatives traded on Ukraine jumped to $9.0 billion in gross notional volumes in the week to Aug 27, up more than 40-fold from $211 million the week before, according to the \uc2 Depository Trust & Clearing Corporation\uc2  (DTCC).\par \par \uc2 However, analysts said the surge in volumes reflected a rise in investor appetite for Ukraine's debt following the resumption of financing from the International Monetary Fund (IMF) last month and resulting credit ratings upgrades.\par \par \uc2 Five-year Ukraine credit default swaps (CDS) <UAGV5YUSAC=MP> nudged higher this week following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reshuffle, but the cost of insuring the country's sovereign debt has fallen to below 600 bps since late August. [ID:nLDE6820PG]\par \par \uc2 At the start of the week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had actually offered to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , last setting the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level at 7.8889 per dollar on Aug. 31, weaker than the previous day's close of 7.8850.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave a signal for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's weakening," said a chief dealer at a Western bank in Kiev.\par \par \uc2 A trader at a local bank said Friday's round of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely bridge the short-term dollar supply gap and help the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilise.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  simply sold dollars to Naftogaz. I don't see any reasons for swift market movements," the trader said.\par \par \uc2 ING said in the medium term it did not expect the reshuffle to affect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy, although the bank does not expect any more \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation this year.\par \par \uc2 Arbuzov's appointment comes as Ukraine's government moves towards boosting the power of Yanukovich, pledging to reverse curbs on presidential authority passed under his predecessor. [ID:nLDE6811U7] (Additional reporting by Andrey Ostroukh and Vladimir Soldatkin in Moscow and Sebastian Tong in London; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 HRYVNIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100903e693000mf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
